==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|endictment}}

===Etymology===
18th century Latinized respelling of {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|endytement||action of accusing}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|enditement}}, from {{m|fro|enditer}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪnˈdaɪt.mənt/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-indictment.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|legal}} An official formal [[accusation]] for a criminal [[offence]], or the process by which it is brought to a [[jury]]. {{defdate|from 14th c.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The official legal document outlining the [[charge]]s concerned. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} An [[accusation]] of wrongdoing; a [[criticism]] or [[condemnation]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}

